# Cloudflare Pages redirect rules. The deploy output is the repo root, so every committed file is
# otherwise served publicly. These paths are dev/build tooling that the live wallet never loads;
# redirect them to the app so they are not served from the production origin. (Pages _redirects has
# no 404 status - only 301/302/303/307/308 - and a redirect is always followed even when the file
# exists, so a 302-to-root is the supported way to stop serving a committed file.)
#
# Kept intentionally public: tests.html / tests.js (a CSP-clean in-browser crypto self-verification
# page), the vendored runtime deps, and the MWEB runtime (mweb.mjs + mweb-node.mjs + their
# noble-sha512 dep), which is now wired into the wallet.

/tools/*                    /  302
